<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>260611 Meeting — PDBbind 2020 Regression</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --ink:        #1c2433;
    --ink-soft:   #5b6678;
    --line:       #e3e7ee;
    --line-strong:#aeb6c4;
    --bg:         #f5f6f8;
    --card:       #ffffff;
    --accent:     #2f6f4f;   /* green for checks / best */
    --best-bg:    #eaf5ee;
    --tbd:        #b07a17;
    --tbd-bg:     #fcf3e0;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .page {
    max-width: 1600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 24px 96px;
  }
  header.doc {
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding-bottom: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  header.doc .date {
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  header.doc h1 {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 650;
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  section.block { margin-bottom: 56px; }
  .table-title {
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 620;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }
  .table-sub {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    max-width: 1080px;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--card);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(20,30,50,.04), 0 8px 24px rgba(20,30,50,.05);
  }
  table.results {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  table.results th, table.results td {
    padding: 11px 9px;
    text-align: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* header */
  table.results thead th {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: #fafbfc;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  table.results thead tr.grp th {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: .1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-weight: 600;
    padding-top: 13px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
  }
  table.results thead tr.grp2 th {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    padding-top: 6px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
  }
  table.results thead tr.grp2 th i { font-style: italic; font-weight: 500; }
  table.results thead tr.sub th {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    letter-spacing: .02em;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 11px;
  }
  /* method column */
  .col-method { text-align: left !important; min-width: 170px; }
  thead .col-method { vertical-align: middle; }
  td.col-method { font-weight: 560; }
  td.col-method .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: .04em;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    margin-left: 7px;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .tag.supervised { background: #eef1f6; color: #5b6678; }
  .tag.inprog { background: var(--tbd-bg); color: var(--tbd); }

  /* positional-encoding pills */
  .col-pe { min-width: 74px; }
  .pe { display: inline-block; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .02em;
        padding: 2px 9px; border-radius: 999px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pe.rope  { background: var(--best-bg); color: #1d5a3a; }
  .pe.learn { background: #eef1f6; color: #5b6678; }

  /* the vertical division between INPUT block and METRICS block */
  .div-major { border-left: 2.5px solid var(--line-strong); }
  /* lighter division between validation and test */
  .div-minor { border-left: 1px dashed var(--line-strong); }

  table.results tbody tr { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  table.results tbody tr:hover { background: #fbfcfd; }

  /* check icons */
  .chk {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 15px; height: 15px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 9px;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .no { color: var(--line-strong); font-size: 14px; }

  /* metric cells */
  .metric { font-size: 14.5px; }
  .metric .val { font-weight: 560; }
  .metric .sd { color: #9aa3b2; font-size: 10.5px; font-weight: 400; }
  td.best { background: var(--best-bg); }
  td.best .val { font-weight: 720; color: #1d5a3a; }
  .tbd {
    color: var(--tbd);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .notes {
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 1080px;
  }
  .notes b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .notes ul { margin: 6px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  .notes li { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .legend {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 18px;
    margin-top: 14px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-soft);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; }
  .placeholder {
    border: 1.5px dashed var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 28px;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 14px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,#fff,#fff 12px,#fafbfc 12px,#fafbfc 24px);
  }

  /* figure cards (gradmag pipeline, dataset filtering) */
  .figure-wrap {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--card);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(20,30,50,.04), 0 8px 24px rgba(20,30,50,.05);
    padding: 20px 20px 14px;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .figure-img { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 760px; height: auto; }
  .figure-img.wide { min-width: 1040px; }
  .figure-cap {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .notes code, .figure-cap code, .table-sub code {
    background: #f0f2f5; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 12.5px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">

  <header class="doc">
    <div class="date">2026 · 06 · 11 — Meeting</div>
    <h1>PDBbind 2020 — Binding-Affinity Regression</h1>
  </header>

  <!-- ============================ TABLE 1 ============================ -->
  <section class="block">
    <p class="table-title">Table 1 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Input ablation on the affinity regression task</p>
    <p class="table-sub">
      LP-PDBBind <code>new_split</code>, frozen-probe (MLP head on frozen pretrained encoder).
      VoxBind rows: mean&nbsp;±&nbsp;std over 3 seeds, identical split
      (n<sub>train</sub>&nbsp;=&nbsp;2172 / n<sub>val</sub>&nbsp;=&nbsp;480 / n<sub>test</sub>&nbsp;=&nbsp;839).
    </p>

    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="results">
        <thead>
          <tr class="grp">
            <th class="col-method" rowspan="3">Experiment</th>
            <th class="col-pe" rowspan="3">PE</th>
            <th colspan="7">Input information</th>
            <th class="div-major" colspan="2">Validation</th>
            <th class="div-minor" colspan="3">Test</th>
          </tr>
          <tr class="grp2">
            <th colspan="2">Pocket</th>
            <th colspan="2">Ligand</th>
            <th rowspan="2">Density</th>
            <th rowspan="2">Gradmag</th>
            <th rowspan="2">H&#8209;bond</th>
            <th class="div-major" rowspan="2">Pearson&nbsp;<i>r</i></th>
            <th rowspan="2">Spearman&nbsp;&rho;</th>
            <th class="div-minor" rowspan="2">Pearson&nbsp;<i>r</i></th>
            <th rowspan="2">Spearman&nbsp;&rho;</th>
            <th rowspan="2">RMSD</th>
          </tr>
          <tr class="sub">
            <th>coords</th>
            <th>atom&nbsp;type</th>
            <th>coords</th>
            <th>atom&nbsp;type</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>

          <!-- Row 1: density + gradmag only -->
          <tr>
            <td class="col-method">Density + gradmag only</td>
            <td><span class="pe learn">ViT</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-major"><span class="val">0.509</span> <span class="sd">±0.005</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.502</span> <span class="sd">±0.001</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-minor"><span class="val">0.513</span> <span class="sd">±0.007</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.505</span> <span class="sd">±0.006</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">1.567</span> <span class="sd">±0.027</span></td>
          </tr>

          <!-- Row 2: coordinates only -->
          <tr>
            <td class="col-method">Coordinates only</td>
            <td><span class="pe learn">ViT</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-major"><span class="val">0.548</span> <span class="sd">±0.001</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.538</span> <span class="sd">±0.001</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-minor"><span class="val">0.557</span> <span class="sd">±0.003</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.544</span> <span class="sd">±0.003</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">1.528</span> <span class="sd">±0.054</span></td>
          </tr>

          <!-- Row 3a: coordinates + density + gradmag, ViT PE -->
          <tr>
            <td class="col-method">Coordinates + density + gradmag</td>
            <td><span class="pe learn">ViT</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-major"><span class="val">0.592</span> <span class="sd">±0.002</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.580</span> <span class="sd">±0.000</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-minor"><span class="val">0.609</span> <span class="sd">±0.008</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.595</span> <span class="sd">±0.006</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">1.430</span> <span class="sd">±0.009</span></td>
          </tr>

          <!-- Row 3b: coordinates + density + gradmag, 3D RoPE (best) -->
          <tr>
            <td class="col-method">Coordinates + density + gradmag</td>
            <td><span class="pe rope">3D&nbsp;RoPE</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-major"><span class="val">0.612</span> <span class="sd">±0.001</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.598</span> <span class="sd">±0.001</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-minor best"><span class="val">0.624</span> <span class="sd">±0.005</span></td>
            <td class="metric best"><span class="val">0.606</span> <span class="sd">±0.004</span></td>
            <td class="metric best"><span class="val">1.398</span> <span class="sd">±0.009</span></td>
          </tr>

          <!-- Row 4: HBGSA (external fully-supervised baseline, full 4-branch) -->
          <tr>
            <td class="col-method">HBGSA<sup>&dagger;</sup> <span class="tag supervised">supervised</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-major"><span class="val">0.508</span> <span class="sd">±0.030</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.519</span> <span class="sd">±0.028</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-minor"><span class="val">0.502</span> <span class="sd">±0.035</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.492</span> <span class="sd">±0.031</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">1.597</span> <span class="sd">±0.033</span></td>
          </tr>

        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="legend">
      <span><span class="chk">&#10003;</span> input used</span>
      <span><span class="no" style="padding:0 4px">&ndash;</span> input not used</span>
      <span><span style="background:var(--best-bg);padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;color:#1d5a3a">bold</span> best test value</span>
    </div>

    <div class="notes">
      <ul>
        <li><b>Common split.</b> All VoxBind rows are evaluated on the same LP-PDBBind
          <code>new_split</code> test set (n&nbsp;=&nbsp;839); numbers are directly comparable.</li>
        <li><b>Best model.</b> Coordinates + density + gradmag (RoPE-3D encoder) is best on every
          test metric — density&nbsp;+&nbsp;gradmag adds <b>+0.062</b> test&nbsp;&rho; on top of coordinates alone.</li>
        <li><b>PE</b> = the encoder's positional encoding. <i>ViT</i> = the original ViT learned-absolute
          embedding; <i>3D RoPE</i> = axial 3D rotary (relative, parameter-free). With the inputs held
          fixed (coordinates + density + gradmag), switching ViT&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;3D RoPE lifts test&nbsp;&rho;
          from 0.595 to 0.606 (<b>+0.011</b>) — so a small part of the best row's edge is the PE, not the
          inputs. HBGSA has no voxel PE.</li>
        <li><b>Density + gradmag only</b> (no coordinate channels) trails coordinates-only by ~0.04&nbsp;&rho; —
          on its own the density signal is informative but weaker than atom geometry.</li>
        <li><b>HBGSA</b> is an external <b>fully-supervised</b> baseline (full 4-branch: H-bond graph +
          protein sequence + binding pocket + ligand SMILES; no voxel/density inputs), 3 seeds,
          model-selected on validation Spearman. On the matched split it reaches test&nbsp;&rho;&nbsp;0.492 —
          <b>below all three VoxBind variants</b> (density+gradmag-only&nbsp;0.505, coordinates-only&nbsp;0.544,
          combined&nbsp;0.606) — i.e. a dedicated supervised model does not beat the frozen VoxBind
          representation on this split.</li>
        <li><sup>&dagger;</sup><b>Split note.</b> HBGSA (4-branch) is trained and scored on the <b>same</b>
          split as the VoxBind rows (restricted to the identical 839-test IDs). It is evaluated on
          n<sub>test</sub>&nbsp;=&nbsp;835 — 4 of the 839 are dropped because RDKit cannot parse their SMILES,
          which HBGSA requires but the voxel models do not. Numbers are the mean over 3 seeds.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ TABLE 2 (placeholder) ============================ -->
  <!--
    To add another table, copy the <section class="block"> ... </section> block above.
    The header structure (Experiment | Input information ×4 | Validation ×2 | Test ×3),
    the .div-major / .div-minor dividers, the .chk / .no icons, and the .best highlight
    are all reusable as-is.
  -->
  <section class="block">
    <p class="table-title">Table 2 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Input ablation on the H-bond-count regression task</p>
    <p class="table-sub">
      Same frozen-probe setup as Table 1 (MLP head on the frozen pretrained encoder; mean&nbsp;&plusmn;&nbsp;std
      over 3 seeds), but the regression target is now the <b>protein&ndash;ligand H-bond count</b>
      (HBGSA geometric criterion: N/O/S donor&ndash;acceptor &le;&nbsp;3.5&nbsp;&#8491; and D&ndash;H&middot;&middot;&middot;A
      &ge;&nbsp;120&deg;, capped at 20). Identical LP-PDBBind <code>new_split</code> as Table 1's VoxBind rows,
      restricted to complexes that carry an H-bond label
      (n<sub>train</sub>&nbsp;=&nbsp;2133 / n<sub>val</sub>&nbsp;=&nbsp;478 / n<sub>test</sub>&nbsp;=&nbsp;835).
      The <b>H-bond column is the regression target here, not an input</b> &mdash; so it is &ndash; for every row.
      RMSE is in H-bond units. (Rows&nbsp;1&ndash;3 are the plain-v5 / learnable-PE family, PE-matched; row&nbsp;4 is
      the RoPE-3D combined encoder &mdash; Table 1's best affinity encoder &mdash; added for a direct cross-table match.)
    </p>

    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="results">
        <thead>
          <tr class="grp">
            <th class="col-method" rowspan="3">Experiment</th>
            <th class="col-pe" rowspan="3">PE</th>
            <th colspan="7">Input information</th>
            <th class="div-major" colspan="2">Validation</th>
            <th class="div-minor" colspan="3">Test</th>
          </tr>
          <tr class="grp2">
            <th colspan="2">Pocket</th>
            <th colspan="2">Ligand</th>
            <th rowspan="2">Density</th>
            <th rowspan="2">Gradmag</th>
            <th rowspan="2">H&#8209;bond<br><span style="font-weight:400;font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-soft)">(target)</span></th>
            <th class="div-major" rowspan="2">Pearson&nbsp;<i>r</i></th>
            <th rowspan="2">Spearman&nbsp;&rho;</th>
            <th class="div-minor" rowspan="2">Pearson&nbsp;<i>r</i></th>
            <th rowspan="2">Spearman&nbsp;&rho;</th>
            <th rowspan="2">RMSE</th>
          </tr>
          <tr class="sub">
            <th>coords</th>
            <th>atom&nbsp;type</th>
            <th>coords</th>
            <th>atom&nbsp;type</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>

          <!-- Row 1: density + gradmag only -->
          <tr>
            <td class="col-method">Density + gradmag only</td>
            <td><span class="pe learn">ViT</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-major"><span class="val">0.708</span> <span class="sd">±0.008</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.603</span> <span class="sd">±0.003</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-minor"><span class="val">0.657</span> <span class="sd">±0.004</span></td>
            <td class="metric best"><span class="val">0.573</span> <span class="sd">±0.004</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">2.379</span> <span class="sd">±0.048</span></td>
          </tr>

          <!-- Row 2: coordinates only -->
          <tr>
            <td class="col-method">Coordinates only</td>
            <td><span class="pe learn">ViT</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-major"><span class="val">0.640</span> <span class="sd">±0.010</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.555</span> <span class="sd">±0.011</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-minor best"><span class="val">0.685</span> <span class="sd">±0.004</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.570</span> <span class="sd">±0.009</span></td>
            <td class="metric best"><span class="val">2.223</span> <span class="sd">±0.186</span></td>
          </tr>

          <!-- Row 3: coordinates + density + gradmag (plain v5 / learnable PE) -->
          <tr>
            <td class="col-method">Coordinates + density + gradmag</td>
            <td><span class="pe learn">ViT</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-major"><span class="val">0.707</span> <span class="sd">±0.001</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.656</span> <span class="sd">±0.001</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-minor"><span class="val">0.672</span> <span class="sd">±0.001</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.559</span> <span class="sd">±0.004</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">2.261</span> <span class="sd">±0.119</span></td>
          </tr>

          <!-- Row 3b: coordinates + density + gradmag (RoPE-3D) = Table 1 best affinity encoder -->
          <tr>
            <td class="col-method">Coordinates + density + gradmag</td>
            <td><span class="pe rope">3D&nbsp;RoPE</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-major"><span class="val">0.692</span> <span class="sd">±0.004</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.645</span> <span class="sd">±0.000</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-minor"><span class="val">0.673</span> <span class="sd">±0.004</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.564</span> <span class="sd">±0.002</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">2.236</span> <span class="sd">±0.092</span></td>
          </tr>

          <!-- Row 4: trivial baseline (ligand polar-atom count) -->
          <tr>
            <td class="col-method">Ligand N/O/S count <span class="tag supervised">baseline</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="chk">&#10003;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td><span class="no">&ndash;</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-major"><span class="val">0.529</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.556</span></td>
            <td class="metric div-minor"><span class="val">0.416</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">0.363</span></td>
            <td class="metric"><span class="val">2.755</span></td>
          </tr>

        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="legend">
      <span><span class="chk">&#10003;</span> input used</span>
      <span><span class="no" style="padding:0 4px">&ndash;</span> input not used</span>
      <span><span style="background:var(--best-bg);padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;color:#1d5a3a">bold</span> best test value (encoders)</span>
    </div>

    <div class="notes">
      <ul>
        <li><b>All encoders clear the trivial baseline by a wide margin.</b> Test&nbsp;&rho;&nbsp;&asymp;&nbsp;0.57
          vs the ligand-N/O/S-count baseline's 0.363 (<b>+0.21</b>) &mdash; the frozen representations encode
          protein&ndash;ligand interaction structure well beyond the ligand's own polar-atom count; they are
          not merely counting ligand N/O/S atoms.</li>
        <li><b>The affinity ordering collapses on this target.</b> On affinity (Table 1) the ranking was clear
          (coords+density+gradmag&nbsp;0.606 &gt; coords&nbsp;0.544 &gt; density+gradmag&nbsp;0.505). On H-bond
          count all four encoders are <b>statistically tied</b> (0.573 / 0.570 / 0.564 / 0.559, within ~2&sigma;)
          &mdash; even the RoPE-3D combined encoder (Table 1's best) reaches only 0.564. Density+gradmag
          <b>alone</b>, with no atom-coordinate channels, predicts H-bonds as well as the full model.</li>
        <li><b>Density carries the H-bond signal; coordinates add nothing here.</b> Mechanistically sensible:
          H-bonds are a property of polar-contact electron density and geometry, which the density+gradmag
          channels encode directly; adding atom-type/coordinate channels buys no test&nbsp;&rho;.</li>
        <li><b>The combined models over-fit validation.</b> The plain-v5 combined has the <i>highest</i>
          val&nbsp;&rho; (0.656) but a low test&nbsp;&rho; (0.559) &mdash; a ~0.10 val&rarr;test gap (the RoPE-3D
          combined behaves the same: 0.645&rarr;0.564), vs near-zero gap for density-only and coords-only.
          Consistent with the &ldquo;density over-fits val&rdquo; pattern seen on affinity.</li>
        <li><b>Caveats.</b> Row&nbsp;4 (RoPE-3D) uses the identical encoder as Table 1's best affinity row, so
          its H-bond &rho; (0.564) <i>is</i> directly cross-comparable &mdash; and confirms the PE that won on
          affinity buys nothing here. The baseline is a deterministic 1-feature linear fit (no seed variance);
          the H-bond label is a geometric N/O/S criterion (no donor/acceptor chemistry), capped at 20.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ FIGURE 1 — gradmag ============================ -->
  <section class="block">
    <p class="table-title">Figure 1 &nbsp;·&nbsp; How the gradient-magnitude (gradmag) channel is computed</p>
    <p class="table-sub">
      Per-voxel <code>&#8214;&nabla;&rho;&#8214;</code> of the normalized electron density — an
      edge / iso-surface detector that fires on atom-blob shells and 2Fo&ndash;Fc contours,
      complementing the raw density magnitude.
    </p>
    <div class="figure-wrap">
      <img class="figure-img"
           alt="Gradient-magnitude pipeline: density rho, three central-difference partials, L2-norm magnitude, per-sample z-score channel"
           src="data:image/png;base64,"/>
    </div>
    <div class="notes">
      <ul>
        <li><b>Input &rho;.</b> The normalized 2Fo&ndash;Fc electron-density crop (v5: arcsinh
          soft-squash + z-score), a 64&sup3; grid at 0.25&nbsp;&Aring;/voxel — the same density
          channel fed to the encoder.</li>
        <li><b>Gradient.</b> Central finite differences along each axis,
          &part;&rho;&nbsp;&asymp;&nbsp;(&rho;<sub>+1</sub>&nbsp;&minus;&nbsp;&rho;<sub>&minus;1</sub>)/2,
          with one voxel of <i>replicate</i> padding so the 64&sup3; shape and boundary faces
          are preserved.</li>
        <li><b>Magnitude.</b> The three partials are combined per voxel by the L2 norm,
          &#8214;&nabla;&rho;&#8214;&nbsp;=&nbsp;&radic;(&part;<sub>x</sub>&rho;&sup2;&nbsp;+&nbsp;&part;<sub>y</sub>&rho;&sup2;&nbsp;+&nbsp;&part;<sub>z</sub>&rho;&sup2;&nbsp;+&nbsp;&epsilon;),
          &epsilon;&nbsp;=&nbsp;1e&minus;12 — large where the density changes fastest.</li>
        <li><b>Normalization.</b> A per-sample z-score (subtract spatial mean, divide by spatial
          std) standardizes the volume; the result is appended as the trailing <b>gradmag</b>
          input channel.</li>
        <li><b>Source.</b> <code>gradient_magnitude3d</code> + <code>per_sample_zscore</code> in
          <code>voxbind/models/density_mae.py</code>; example rendered on PDBbind entry
          <code>1bcd</code> (densest z-slice).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ FIGURE 2 — dataset pipeline ============================ -->
  <section class="block">
    <p class="table-title">Figure 2 &nbsp;·&nbsp; PDBbind 2020 &rarr; affinity-regression dataset (filtering pipeline)</p>
    <p class="table-sub">
      From the deposited refined set down to the labeled train / val / test splits used in Table&nbsp;1.
    </p>
    <div class="figure-wrap">
      <img class="figure-img wide"
           alt="PDBbind 2020 filtering funnel: refined 5,316, supported elements 4,042, electron density 3,664, labeled and split, train/val/test 2,172/480/839"
           src="data:image/png;base64,"/>
    </div>
    <div class="notes">
      <ul>
        <li><b>Start.</b> PDBbind 2020 <b>refined set</b> — 5,316 complexes with deposited protein +
          pocket + ligand structures (of 19,443 entries in the LP-PDBBind index).</li>
        <li><b>Supported elements.</b> &minus;1,274 complexes with unsupported non-H atoms (pocket
          metals Zn/Mg/Ca, ligand halogens Br/I) &rarr; 4,042 atom-voxelized (11-channel 64&sup3; grids).</li>
        <li><b>Electron density.</b> &minus;378 with no PDBe 2Fo&ndash;Fc map &rarr; 3,664
          density-bearing complexes — the pool for any density / gradmag condition.</li>
        <li><b>Label &amp; split.</b> Drop covalent + unlabeled, then assign the LP-PDBBind
          leakage-controlled <code>new_split</code> &rarr; 2,172 / 480 / 839 (train / val / test).</li>
        <li><b>CL1 refresh (2026-06-10).</b> Restricting the 3,664-pool to LP-PDBBind's cleanest
          leakage level (CL1) gives 1,698 / 437 / 785 — the split HBGSA is scored on.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ FIGURE 3 — HBGSA channels ============================ -->
  <section class="block">
    <p class="table-title">Figure 3 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; HBGSA &mdash; the four input channels for affinity prediction</p>
    <p class="table-sub">
      Our standalone reimplementation of HBGSA (arXiv&nbsp;2604.23115, Fig.&nbsp;1) in
      <code>hbgsa_baseline/</code>. Four supervised input channels, each encoded to a
      128-d embedding, concatenated and regressed to the binding affinity p<i>K</i>.
    </p>
    <div class="figure-wrap">
      <img class="figure-img wide"
           alt="HBGSA four input channels: H-bond graph, protein sequence, binding pocket, ligand SMILES, each to a 128-d embedding, concatenated to 512 and regressed via an MLP head to predicted pK"
           src="data:image/png;base64,"/>
    </div>
    <div class="notes">
      <ul>
        <li><b><code>s_hb</code> &mdash; H-bond graph</b> (paper core). Up to 20 protein&ndash;ligand
          H-bonds become graph nodes (criteria d&nbsp;&le;&nbsp;3.5&nbsp;&Aring;, D&ndash;H&middot;&middot;&middot;A&nbsp;&ge;&nbsp;120&deg;,
          polar&nbsp;N/O/S). Each node is a 9-d vector
          [&nbsp;protein-end&nbsp;xyz&nbsp;|&nbsp;ligand-end&nbsp;xyz&nbsp;|&nbsp;midpoint&nbsp;xyz&nbsp;];
          dynamic&nbsp;KNN (k&nbsp;=&nbsp;5) over midpoints builds edges &rarr; 2&times;&nbsp;<code>GCNConv</code>
          + residual &rarr; global max-pool.</li>
        <li><b><code>v_seq</code> &mdash; protein sequence.</b> Per-residue 9-d physicochemical
          descriptors (Kyte-Doolittle, Hopp-Woods, flexibility, accessibility, Janin, charge,
          polarity, aromaticity, MW) &rarr; linear &rarr; 2&times; Transformer self-attention &rarr;
          masked mean.</li>
        <li><b><code>v_pkt</code> &mdash; binding pocket.</b> Pocket residues (&le;&nbsp;128) read from
          <code>{pdb}_pocket.pdb</code>, same per-residue descriptors &rarr; 1D convolution
          (kernel&nbsp;3) &rarr; masked max-pool.</li>
        <li><b><code>v_smi</code> &mdash; ligand SMILES.</b> Atom-level regex tokens (&le;&nbsp;200,
          Schwaller pattern) &rarr; token embedding &rarr; 2&times; Transformer self-attention &rarr;
          masked mean.</li>
        <li><b>Fusion &amp; loss.</b> concat(4&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;128&nbsp;=&nbsp;512) &rarr; FC
          512&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;128&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;64&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;1 &rarr; p<i>K</i>;
          loss&nbsp;=&nbsp;SmoothL1&nbsp;+&nbsp;50&middot;(1&nbsp;&minus;&nbsp;Pearson&nbsp;r), with the target
          p<i>K</i> z-standardized on train and de-standardized for RMSE.</li>
        <li><b>Read it as.</b> HBGSA is a <i>fully-supervised, end-to-end</i> model &mdash; an external
          reference (Table&nbsp;1), not a representation probe like the frozen VoxBind rows.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ FIGURE 4 — xray pipeline ============================ -->
  <section class="block">
    <p class="table-title">Figure 4 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; From experimental data to atomic coordinates &mdash; the crystallography pipeline</p>
    <p class="table-sub">
      Where the electron density we train on comes from, and why VoxBind taps it directly.
      Redraw of <code>figures/xray&nbsp;pipeline.png</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="figure-wrap">
      <img class="figure-img wide"
           alt="Crystallography pipeline: protein crystal, X-ray diffraction, 2Fo-Fc electron-density map, fitted atomic model; VoxBind learns from the density field directly"
           src="data:image/png;base64,"/>
    </div>
    <div class="notes">
      <ul>
        <li><b>Crystal &rarr; diffraction.</b> An ordered crystal scatters X-rays into discrete
          reflections; the detector records intensities&nbsp;|F|&sup2; (the phases are lost &mdash; the
          crystallographic <i>phase problem</i>).</li>
        <li><b>Diffraction &rarr; density.</b> After phasing, a Fourier synthesis reconstructs the
          <b>2Fo&ndash;Fc electron-density map</b> &rho;(x,&nbsp;y,&nbsp;z) &mdash; the last fully
          experimental object in the chain.</li>
        <li><b>Density &rarr; model.</b> Atomic coordinates are then <i>fitted into</i> the density by
          human / automated model-building, which introduces geometry priors and regularization.</li>
        <li><b>Why it matters here.</b> VoxBind learns from the density field itself (and its
          gradient magnitude, Fig.&nbsp;1), complementing models that only see the downstream
          fitted coordinates.</li>
        <li><b>Source.</b> Stage&nbsp;3 is a real PDBe 2Fo&ndash;Fc crop (<code>1bcd</code>, densest
          z-slice); stages&nbsp;1,&nbsp;2,&nbsp;4 are schematic icons.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
</body>
</html>
